text.en:
This Act shall apply to a child of compulsory religious school age —

(a) who is a Muslim;

(b) who is born on or after 1st January 2006;

(c) who is residing in Brunei Darussalam; and

(d) whose parent, at least one of whom, is a citizen of Brunei Darussalam or a permanent resident. Exclusive jurisdiction of Syariah Courts.

(1) There is hereby established a body known as the Compulsory Religious Education Board.

(2) The Board shall comprise —

(a) the Deputy Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Religious Affairs, to be the chairman;

(b) the Director of Islamic Studies, to be the deputy chairman;

(c) not less than seven members to be appointed by the

(d) the Assistant Director of Islamic Studies, to be the secretary.
